' EXPLORER.SPK - Explorer, the file manager as Windows 95 has it: the folders
' in a tree on the left, what's in one on the right as icons, a list or
' details, and the network in the same window. Map another machine's disk as
' a drive letter (Tools > Map Network Drive: Z: is \\BRAVO\MYFILES) and it's in
' the tree under My Computer, next to (C:), every time Explorer starts.
'
'   EXPLORER.SPK                  opens My Computer... or the folder given:
'   EXPLORER.SPK C:\MYFILES       EXPLORER.SPK \\BRAVO\       EXPLORER.SPK Z:\
'   EXPLORER.SPK /folder C:\DOCS  a folder window, without the tree
'
' Copy, Cut and Paste work between Explorer windows (C:\SYSTEM\EXPCLIP.TXT),
' and between machines; so do dragging files onto a folder (a move on the
' same disk, a copy to another one, as Windows does it; drag with the right
' button to choose). Deleting from C: goes to the Recycle Bin (C:\RECYCLED).
' A file on another machine opens in a copy here, and what you save goes back.
'
' Built from explorer/src: MAIN (this), VFS (paths, the network, drives, the
' Recycle Bin), VIEW (drawing the tree and the files, the mouse and keys),
' ACTIONS (what the menus do, and the dialogs) and the icons, which
' tools/build-installer.mjs makes from explorer/src/ICONS.TXT.

CONST ME = "C:\PROGRAMS\EXPLORER.SPK"
CONST DRIVESFILE = "C:\SYSTEM\DRIVES.INI"
CONST PWLFILE = "C:\SYSTEM\PASSWORD.PWL"
CONST CLIPFILE = "C:\SYSTEM\EXPCLIP.TXT"
CONST SETFILE = "C:\SYSTEM\EXPLORER.INI"
CONST BINDIR = "C:\RECYCLED"
CONST TEMPDIR = "C:\SYSTEM\TEMP"
CONST ROWH = 18
CONST TBH = 30
CONST ADDRH = 26
CONST HEADH = 20
CONST SBW = 16
CONST SPLITW = 5
CONST INDENT = 19

' ---- the window and its controls
VAR win AS GUI_Window
VAR bar AS GUI_Menu
VAR ctx AS GUI_Menu
VAR tb AS GUI_Canvas
VAR combo AS GUI_DropDown
